<<system_line "Layout 4 — the System layout. This card is the title screen's reading card, in the speech bubble's place, and it arrives whole.">>
<<player_line "Layout 4 reply. [[Layouts->Layouts]]">>

:: System content [checker scratch] {"position":"520,750"}
/* A system message exercising the layout: wiki-processed text and a link that
   is clickable as soon as the card appears, because nothing is revealed. The
   reply bar is the way on. Reach it from the browser console:
     SugarCube.Engine.play("System content") */
<<set_layout 4>>
<<system_line "Before the story starts: this is a system message. It is not Cam speaking, so there is no portrait and no speech bubble. Variables and links work here, [[Layouts->Layouts]], and the link is clickable at once.">>
<<player_line "Understood. [[Layout 0->Layout 0]]">>

:: System content long [checker scratch] {"position":"570,750"}
/* A system message longer than the card: scroll it and confirm the card's
   frame stays exactly where it is while the words travel inside it. Reach it
   from the browser console:
     SugarCube.Engine.play("System content long") */
<<set_layout 4>>
<<system_line "This system message is deliberately longer than the card, so the prose has to scroll inside it while the frame stays exactly where it is. Watch the card's edge: it should not move at all. The text should stop at the frame rather than paint over it, and the card's shadow should not fade a single letter. The same card should hold still while the words travel. A link lives in this message too, [[Layouts->Layouts]], and it should be clickable the moment the card appears: nothing here is revealed a character at a time. The message is whole and scrolls like any other card of prose.">>
<<player_line "The long system message has landed. [[Layouts->Layouts]]">>

